Z||000000||Taijiguy||05-02-2001||04:57 PM||||Found this spreadsheet on a good site for carburation info: <A HREF="http://www.parkercarburetion.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.parkercarburetion.com</A>  <BR>The guys name is Earl Parker and has a great deal of knowledge about carbs and tuning, etc. He has some free downloads, and among them, a handy spreadsheet for performing all kind of automotive calculations (not limited to carburation) such as displacement, tire sizes, compression ratios, etc. It's definietly worth having on hand. the link is: <A HREF="http://www.parkercarburetion.com/Excel/RacingFormulas.xls" TARGET=_blank>http://www.parkercarburetion.com/Excel/RacingFormulas.xls</A> <BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
